; error: 6:3: wrapper 'logged' takes 'R' from a task value, where it is [int]@?, in a region that task value takes; which region that is only the body of 'logged' says, when it gives the task value one, so 'R' can't be in it; write that type out in the header of 'logged', with the region it takes, as in '(next: (@a, int) -> [int]@a, a: region, n: int) -> [int]@a'
; A generic wrapper can't find what it sends in a region the task value takes: which one its body gives is not known at the use.
task logged<R>(next: (@a, @b, int) -> R, a: region, b: region, n: int) -> R
    <- next(a, b, n)
fi
$(logged)
task cubes(s: region, r: region, n: int) -> [int]@s
    hold made = new [int]() at s
    made.add(n)
    <- made
fi
task main()
    region outer
    hold keep = new [int]() at outer
    block
        region inner
        keep = cubes(inner, outer, 3)
    fi
    region other
    hold junk = new [int]() at other
    each i in 0..1000
        junk.add(i)
    fi
    show(keep)
fi
